<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The respondent's counter-schedule of loss for 1002.2 (Employment Tribunal, Mr K Stott), dated 19 October 2026.

  Every result is a real formula, and each formula cell also carries the value it works out to (office:value),
  which LibreOffice shows until it recalculates. If a figure changes, change the cached value beside it.
  The sums, for checking by hand:

    claimant:    basic 7 x 540 = 3,780; lost earnings 11.5 x 440 = 5,060; continuing 52 x 60 = 3,120; statutory rights 500
                 compensatory 5,060 + 3,120 + 500 = 8,680; no reductions; total 3,780 + 8,680 = 12,460
    respondent:  basic 7 x 540 = 3,780; lost earnings 4.4 x 440 = 1,936; continuing 13 x 60 = 780; statutory rights 400
                 compensatory 1,936 + 780 + 400 = 3,116; less 25% (779.00) = 2,337.00
                 conduct 50%: basic 3,780 -> 1,890.00; compensatory 2,337.00 -> 1,168.50; total 3,058.50
    difference:  12,460.00 - 3,058.50 = 9,401.50
-->
