        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="8"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rowDiff"><table:table-cell table:style-name="Diff" table:number-columns-spanned="7" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Difference between the two schedules (claimant’s total less respondent’s total)</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="6"/><table:table-cell table:style-name="DiffMoney" table:formula="of:=[.D24]-[.H24]" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="9401.5"><text:p>£9,401.50</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="8"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Heading" table:number-columns-spanned="8" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Notes</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="7"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rowNote3"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="8" office:value-type="string"><text:p>1.  Mr Stott was dismissed on 12 June 2026 and was paid seven weeks’ pay in lieu of notice, which took him to 31 July 2026. The respondent counts lost earnings only for August: 4.4 weeks. The claimant counts 11.5 weeks from 12 June.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="7"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rowNote3"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="8" office:value-type="string"><text:p>2.  Mr Stott started a new job on 1 September 2026 at £380 net a week, which is £60 a week less than the £440 he earned with the respondent. The respondent allows 13 weeks’ continuing loss; the claimant claims 52.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="7"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rowNote3"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="8" office:value-type="string"><text:p>3.  The respondent takes 25% off the compensatory award because he would have been dismissed anyway, and then 50% off both awards for his own conduct. The claimant allows no reduction. Figures are before interest, and are not an admission that the dismissal was unfair.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="7"/></table:table-row>
      </table:table>
    </office:spreadsheet>
  </office:body>
</office:document>
